Third-Party Code Notice
=======================

This directory (`src/gssc/_improved_diffusion/`) is a fork of vendored
third-party code that is NOT part of the GSSC-S2D2 project itself. It is
redistributed here under its original licenses, separate from the MIT
license that governs the rest of this repository (see the root LICENSE).

FOUR distinct upstream projects are represented here, not one. An earlier
version of this file declared only improved-diffusion for the whole
directory; the complete record, with the measured overlap for each file, is
in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md at the repository root.

Upstream project 1 -- improved-diffusion (most of this directory)
-----------------------------------------------------------------

  Name:    improved-diffusion
  Source:  https://github.com/openai/improved-diffusion
  Paper:   "Improved Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Models"
           Alex Nichol, Prafulla Dhariwal. ICML 2021.
           arXiv:2102.09672  (https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.09672)
  Code authors / copyright holders:
           OpenAI
  License: MIT (full text below). Upstream publishes a LICENSE file, and
           the copyright notice below is the one it carries.

  Covers gaussian_diffusion.py, nn.py, losses.py, resample.py, respace.py,
  script_util.py, train_util.py, unet.py, logger.py, dist_util.py,
  fp16_util.py, image_datasets.py, and the four UNet variants derived from
  upstream unet.py -- unet_sparse.py, unet_multinomial.py, unet_factorized.py
  and unet_old_fullres_baseline.py. The measured overlap for each is in
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md section 4, together with the exact procedure that
  reproduces it. Figures are deliberately NOT duplicated here: they are
  properties of two moving files, and the copies in this file had already
  drifted from the measurement once.

